From 8c031b51ad33ec0c5e6d3655223e9bfc945ff05a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patch-author <a@a.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:01:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0383: Steam leaderboards wired in for real

- Vendored the leaderboard fork (both Linux and Windows builds) into
  electron/steamworks-leaderboards/. package.json's steamworks.js
  dependency now points at it via file: path -- same package name, zero
  changes needed anywhere else that already imports 'steamworks.js'.
- New IPC handlers: steam:uploadGuildPowerScore,
  steam:downloadGuildPowerEntries, steam:getLocalSteamId.
- leaderboard.ts: real async fetchLeaderboard + throttled (5 min)
  uploadGuildPowerScore, called from engine.ts's saveNow(). Falls back
  to the patch-0363 'just your own row' preview whenever Steam can't
  answer.
- LeaderboardModal.tsx: genuinely async now, real loading state,
  refetches on Global/Friends scope change.
- Fixed a real TS2748 (ambient const enum access under isolatedModules)
  by extracting the parameter type instead of referencing the enum's
  value namespace.
- Fixed two real packaging bugs found while verifying: electron-builder
  wasn't following the file: dependency's symlink for .node unpacking
  (fixed via explicit asarUnpack + new .npmrc's install-links=true), and
  a stale package-lock.json was silently overriding the new local path
  (fixed via a genuinely clean node_modules + lockfile reinstall).
- Verified: tsc --noEmit, vite build (steamworks.js still externalized),
  a full electron-builder --linux dir package build, npx asar list
  confirming both .node files land in app.asar.unpacked (not sealed
  inside app.asar), and a real launch under xvfb-run with clean
  graceful-degradation output.
